{
  "description": "HMAC scheme for webhooks in both directions. Inbound ingest expects x-webhook-signature over the exact body bytes. Outbound deliveries (webhook endpoints, incident notifications, alert webhooks) carry X-AxonPush-Timestamp (Unix seconds) and X-AxonPush-Signature-V2 = hex HMAC over timestamp + '.' + body; receivers should reject timestamps more than a few minutes old. The body-only X-AxonPush-Signature is still sent for one release and is deprecated.",
